Day 47/100 of #DrGVishwanathanChallenge

Today I solved LeetCode 104 -Maximum Depth of Binary Tree 
This was a simple problem, but it was a good practice of understanding how recursion works with binary trees.
Approach:
I used DFS + recursion.
For each node, I find the maximum depth of its left and right subtrees and then add 1 for the current node.
If the node is null, I return 0.
So basically:
maxDepth = 1 + max(leftDepth, rightDepth)
Complexity:

Time: O(n) - every node is visited once
Space: O(h) -due to the recursion stack, where h is the height of the tree
The main takeaway for me was understanding how a problem can be broken down into smaller subtrees and solved recursively.
